{{!
    @template block_compass/block

    The block shell: one React mount point, and nothing else of the block's own. Every
    tier, tier 3 included, renders inside the component.

    The mount point's inner content is what the first paint shows until React commits, which
    replaces it (core's mount.ts, createRoot().render()). It holds tier 1's place (ADR-018): the
    calendar's head where the strip renders (block_compass/calendar_skeleton) and tier 1's
    skeleton in the shape it last settled to (block_compass/tier1_skeleton), which React's first
    render draws alike, so the mount swaps like for like. All of it is aria-hidden, and shown only
    under body.jsenabled, which core sets at the top of the body: without JavaScript the two
    sentences below show, as before.

    The props arrive already JSON-encoded from the renderable, in one value, through a
    triple stash: the quote helper corrupts any value carrying a doubled-brace pair, and
    json_encode() in the renderable does not. Nothing between here and React is an HTML
    context, so a double stash would reach the reader as literal entities.

    The section's trailing content is what a reader sees if the component never
    mounts, which is silent apart from a console message. It says the block could not
    load, which is then true, and offers nothing to press. With JavaScript on it waits,
    hidden, behind the skeleton, and a CSS step about 10 s after the first paint swaps the
    two (styles.css, .compass-preload), so no shimmer lasts for ever. Only the mounted
    component renders course cards, so a step asserting a course name asserts that React ran.

    The noscript beside it covers the other way this block shows nothing. With
    JavaScript off both messages appear, and both are true: one says what happened,
    the other says why.

    The mount point names the bundle: one ES module built from Block.tsx by a build step
    outside core's grunt, opted into by js/esm/bundle.json, so the client arrives in one
    request rather than one per module. The per-file outputs stay in js/esm/build for
    core's own build check and are imported by nothing.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * props - the component's props, JSON-encoded by block_compass\output\block:
      labels, icons, strips, favouritesenabled, showsearch, showindex, headinglevel and tier1.
    * tier1 - tier 1's skeleton (block_compass/tier1_skeleton's context).
    * calendarhead - the calendar's head (block_compass/calendar_skeleton's context), or null
      where the strip does not render.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "props": "{\"labels\": {\"loaderror\": \"Your courses could not be loaded.\"}, \"strips\": []}",
        "tier1": {
            "slots": [
                {
                    "strip": {
                        "hastitle": false,
                        "title": "",
                        "later": false,
                        "completion": true,
                        "closing": false,
                        "onerow": true,
                        "cards": [{"card": true}, {"card": true}, {"card": true}]
                    },
                    "note": false
                }
            ],
            "ghostalone": false,
            "empty": false,
            "category": true
        },
        "calendarhead": null
    }
}}
<div class="compass-root" data-region="block_compass">
    {{#react}}
    {
        "component": "@moodle/lms/block_compass/bundle",
        "props": {{{props}}}
    }
    <div class="compass-preload" aria-hidden="true">
        {{#calendarhead}}{{> block_compass/calendar_skeleton}}{{/calendarhead}}
        {{#tier1}}{{> block_compass/tier1_skeleton}}{{/tier1}}
    </div>
    <p class="compass-noscript">{{#str}}loaderror, block_compass{{/str}}</p>
    {{/react}}
    <noscript>
        <p class="compass-noscript">{{#str}}javascriptrequired, block_compass{{/str}}</p>
    </noscript>
</div>
